        <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
          <TrustBadge />
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-3 mb-6 flex-wrap">
          <span class="bg-[#FF5A1F] text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Guide
          </span>
          <span class="bg-green-500 text-white px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">
            Updated October 2026
          </span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
          Best Treadmill Settings <span class="text-[#5AA9FF]">for Fat Loss</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">
          There is no magic number on the console, but there are sensible ones. Here are concrete speed, incline and time settings for four fitness levels, the built-in program worth choosing, what those settings burn by plain arithmetic, and the honest reason the kitchen matters more than the console.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
          <a href="#settings-by-level" class="bg-[#FF5A1F] hover:bg-[#E64F16] text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm">
            Settings by Fitness Level
          </a>
          <a href="#weekly-routine" class="bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white px-8 py-4 rounded-xl font-black no-underline transition-colors uppercase tracking-widest text-sm border border-white/20">
            A Weekly Settings Plan
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>


    <!-- Author & Meta -->
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 pt-12">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 py-8 border-b border-gray-100">
        <img src="/authors/shaheer-ali-khan.png" alt="Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD" width="48" height="48" class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full" />
        <div>
          <p class="font-bold text-gray-900 leading-tight"><a href="/editorial-standards/#who" rel="author" class="text-gray-900 no-underline hover:underline">Shaheer Ali Khan, PhD</a></p>
          <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm leading-tight">Exercise Physiology & Biomechanics Specialist · ACSM-EP, CSCS</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hidden sm:block w-px h-8 bg-gray-200"></div>
        <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm">
          Last Updated: <strong class="text-gray-700">October 14, 2026</strong>
        </p>
        <div class="ml-auto">
          <SocialProof users="1.8k" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="not-prose my-10 bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
        <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 m-0 leading-relaxed">
          <strong class="text-gray-900">What this page is, and is not.</strong> We review treadmills.
          The settings below are general starting points built from published exercise equations and
          common training conventions — they are not medical, coaching or nutrition advice, and we are
          not qualified to give any of those. Weight loss depends far more on diet, sleep, medication
          and health than on any treadmill setting. If you have a heart, lung, joint, metabolic or
          other condition, are pregnant, take medication that affects heart rate (such as beta
          blockers), have an injury, or have not exercised for a long time, talk to a doctor or
          physical therapist before starting, and a registered dietitian for anything about food.
          <strong class="text-gray-900">On the figures below:</strong> MET values come from the ACSM
